			]
		}
		{
			title: "A Bit of FOPGame Server History"
			x: -0.25d
			y: -0.5d
			shape: "gear"
			description: [
				"&7Long ago, Bandit, the FOPGame Server was a much different place. It was your bog standard VR MMO run by the FOP. On its own, it was decently popular, but was used primarily to attract users to the FOP's products and services outside the game."
				""
				"&7At some point, they took the servers offline for a couple months for a 'major update'. At this time, the other big MMO, SBurb, had suddenly closed its doors and the company vanished."
				""
				"&7When the FOPGame Server came back up, it was retooled and had a lot of new systems and items VERY similar to SBurb. The FOPGame Server became a social sci-fi MMO, no longer requiring VR, and became even more popular."
				""
				"&7Hidden in a shareholder report when it had gone offline was that the FOP had acquired the entirety of SBurb and its owning company. They had merged the SBurb code into their own MMO and relaunched."
				""
				"&7Years later, the FOPGame Server would go offline for almost a year before coming back in its current iteration, incorporating a different game called Vault Hunters into it."
			]
			dependencies: ["3EB5B79FC05245E2"]
			size: 0.75d
			id: "116475665151AF8D"
			tasks: [{
				id: "295FAD5263A63CC1"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			x: -0.75d
			y: -0.5d
			description: [
				"&7When the Grand Mall became inacessible, the FOP left in some decoration mods in the files, but never made them accessible to the new FOPGame Server."
				""
				"&7Thus, a large variety of deco items became lost. They are only obtainable by those who visit the Liminal Mall."
				""
				"&7You can also find almost everything you need to survive here, outside of the Overworld of the FOPGame Server. "
			]
			dependencies: ["16A325B14A4EBB16"]
			id: "3EB5B79FC05245E2"
			tasks: [{
				id: "639A75CB84CE0DB8"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
